{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/pulls/15139","id":5243838081,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSVpu_M8AAAABOI6egQ","html_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/pull/15139","diff_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/pull/15139.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/pull/15139.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/issues/15139","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/pulls/15139/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/pulls/15139/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/issues/15139/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JakeChampion/lang/statuses/d5daff9dce5345f73f28f7c784c86d62cf12dcb1","number":15139,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"asm_ir: one window for the last bytes of a mismatch on x86-64, and the bssl interop case","user":{"login":"JakeChampion","id":1569131,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjkxMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1569131?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion","html_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The 2026-11-10 nightly put `net/fern/c64.rps` at 110,273, 1.0% behind zap and 1.4% behind hyper. This PR records the measurements of that gap and makes one cut in the worker's instructions. Part of #12887.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **The x86-64 mismatch kernel finishes in one window** (`compiler/asm_ir.fern`). It compared 16 bytes at a time, then the last 1 to 15 bytes one at a time, at 6 instructions for each byte. Now, for a range of 16 bytes or more, it compares the last 16 bytes in one window. That window ends at the end of the range and can overlap bytes that already compared equal. So the first mismatch that it finds is the first mismatch of the range. The arm64 kernel already finishes with 8, 4 and 2 byte windows.\n- **`TestSelfHostMismatchIR` also checks `__mismatch_bytes_str`**, the form that std/http uses. It checks each length from 0 to 40 with a mismatch at each position, on x86-64, arm64 and wasm.\n- **The TLS interop case against bssl expects the refusal of std/fetch** (`scripts/net-tls-interop`, `scripts/net-tls-interop.d/client.fern`). The 2026-11-10 nightly failed `client against bssl`. Since #15103, a close with no close_notify is `tls.Truncated`, and std/fetch does not let it complete a body that ends at the close (RFC 9112 section 9.8). bssl's `-www` server ends its body at the close and sends no close_notify. The socket cases now keep the bytes before a `Truncated` end and report the end beside the body. So against BoringSSL they still check the handshake, the body, the resumption and the client certificate.\n- **`docs/benchmarks/net-c64-2026-11-10.md`** records the gap. It has the nightly rows of two runs and the worker's instructions at both commits, which are the same within 0.07%. It also has the system calls of each request and the profile of the worker.\n\n## Measured here\n\nThe hello server (`scripts/net-bench.d/hello.fern`) ran under callgrind with `WORKERS=1`, loaded by oha on 64 connections for 60,000 requests:\n\n| | instructions in the worker |\n|---|--:|\n| main e23f590d1 | 522,806,840 |\n| this PR | 518,061,356 |\n\nThat is 79 fewer instructions for each request, 0.91% of the worker. std/http compares each header name and value with the previous request through this kernel.\n\nThe whole x86-64 `scripts/perf-bench` run is inside the 1% tolerance against `.github/perf-baseline.txt`.\n\n## Ran here\n\n- Pass: `TestSelfHostMismatchIRX86_64`, `TestSelfHostMismatchIRArm64` and `TestSelfHostMismatchIRWasm`.\n- Pass: `scripts/perf-bench` on x86-64. No row moved by 1% or more.\n- Pass: the interop client against a `bssl` built at the script's BoringSSL commit. Its output matches the new `expected_client bssl` line for line. That local `bssl` bound IPv4 in place of IPv6, because this machine has no IPv6.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01NrV89WCzyMK6sYJbUTkWTy)_\n\n\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:20:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:12:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6404b67ef4ffde6e7ba55e90bf483666c5faa07d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"JakeChampion:ccr-b4649f9e-lznb5p","ref":"ccr-b4649f9e-lznb5p","repo":{"id":1230663420,"node_id":"R_kgDOSVpu_A","name":"lang","full_name":"JakeChampion/lang","owner":{"login":"JakeChampion","id":1569131,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjkxMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1569131?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion","html_url":"https://github.com/JakeChampion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JakeChampion/subscriptions","organi